    "vocabulary_rule": "a label carried by at least 10 pre-2020 works and by no more than 15% of them: frequent enough to pair, specific enough for the pairing to mean something; at most 20000 survive, the rarest first, and a work contributes at most 16 of them",
    "edge_rule": "two vocabulary concepts share an edge when some work carries both labels; the walker graph counts only pre-2020 works, so an edge there means the combination had already been made",
    "confirmed_rule": "a concept absent from every pre-2020 work, carried by at least 10 post-2020 works, and in the top 10% of post-2020 document frequency: a direction that did not exist at T and then became one",
    "counterexample_rule": "a vocabulary concept used by at least 10 works up to 2017, whose per-work usage rate over the last 3 years before T fell into the steepest-declining 15% of such concepts and to no more than 50% of its earlier rate, with a pre-2020 degree in the top 25% of those: it was well connected and then the field moved off it. Read entirely from pre-2020 data, so the walker could see it too",
    "seed_rule": "the most connected concepts whose pre-2020 document frequency sits between the 40th and 80th percentile of the vocabulary: above that band a concept is generic residue with no topic, below it there is too little structure to walk"
